        <body>
            <div xml:id="d626-a1">

                <pb facs="0747" n="661" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg661"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. McCreery to the collector of customs at El
                        Paso.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-07-17"><hi rendition="#italic">July 17,
                        1903</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: This will introduce to you my friend, Hon.
                    Jumpei Shinabu, chargé d’affaires of Japan, who, after a residence of a year and
                    a half in Mexico, is returning to his own country by way of San Francisco.</p>
                <p>I trust that there will be extended to Mr. Shinabu such courtesies as it is
                    possible to extend to a duly accredited diplomatic representative of a friendly
                    Government. Any courtesies extended to him will be greatly appreciated by
                    me.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully, yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Fenton R. McCreery</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Chargé d’affaires ad interim.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
